slipcase-desktop (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on slipcase-common for the media type and the icon a container is
    drawn with, which this package no longer ships. They have to be declared
    once for every product that opens containers, and two packages cannot
    install the same path. slipcase-common must be in the apt repository before
    or with this version, or the upgrade has an unsatisfiable dependency.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:30:00 -0500

slipcase-desktop (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove a reference to a private Apple graphics function, picked up from the
    window library the application is built on and never called by Slipcase.
    Apple refuses any Mac App Store submission naming one, which is what this
    fixes. It changes nothing on this platform, and no Linux package was built
    from it: v0.1.3 is the tag the macOS submission was cut from.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 07:30:00 -0500

slipcase-desktop (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on libxkbcommon-x11-0, which the application opens by name under the
    X11 display backend and which nothing else in the dependency list pulls in.
    Without it the package installed and the application exited at startup on
    any X11 machine that did not already have the library. A Wayland session
    never loads it, which is why two releases went out with it missing.
  * Start on a Windows machine with no Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable.
    0.1.1 linked the Visual C++ runtime as a separate library and would not
    open without it. Nothing about this package changes: the fix is a Windows
    build setting and 0.1.2 here is 0.1.1 rebuilt.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:15:00 -0500

slipcase-desktop (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show a payload name escaped in the metadata tree as well as on the card.
    A payload called report<U+202E>fdp.exe read report\u{202E}fdp.exe on the
    card and reportfdp.exe in the tree below it, the character that reorders
    text taking no space of its own.
  * Keep the control that removes a key inside the window when the key carries
    a long comment. The comment took whatever width the row had left and the
    control was laid out past the right edge, drawn nowhere and reachable only
    by widening the window. The comment now truncates.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:50:34 -0500

slipcase-desktop (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release. Opens a .slpc container, shows its metadata as an editable
    tree, and hands the payload to whatever the desktop has registered for it.
  * Containers are read and written entirely through the slpc library. This
    application parses none of its own.
  * Installs a media type, a desktop entry, and scalable icons for both the
    application and the container, so a container opens on a double-click.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:18:14 -0500
